 h_chart:"KUB / THB",
 n_tv:"The chart is provided by TradingView from Bitkub's own KUBTHB feed, which carries years of history and a complete set of drawing tools, beyond what the data KUB Flow collects can offer. Every panel below the chart is measured by KUB Flow from its own trade record.",
 w_chart:"Where price has been, at a glance, with the history and drawing tools a chart needs. It answers the direction question so the panels below can answer the ones a price chart cannot: what a trade would cost, who is paying the spread, and where the supply sits.",
 h_tech:"Indicator readings",
 l_tech:"These values are calculated by KUB Flow from the bars it collects, and are not read from the chart above, so they reconcile with the execution-cost, sweep and taker panels below. Each row states where the value sits against its conventional threshold, and how many bars were used. An indicator whose period exceeds the bars collected is reported as unavailable rather than estimated.",
 w_tech:"The standard momentum, trend and volatility readings in one table, each with the number of bars behind it. The bar count is the point: a reading computed from too few bars is shown as unavailable, so a number on this page is never more confident than the data under it.",
