 l_cost:"Bitkub's own book can be dragged to price a sweep by hand, at the current moment. KUB Flow does it automatically at fixed sizes, every five minutes, keeps the series, and puts the result beside the on-chain venues — the value is the history and the comparison, not the arithmetic.",
 w_flow:"What a trade of a given size would actually cost, how that cost has been moving, which side is paying the spread, and which single orders cleared several price levels at once. Together they describe liquidity: a market can look calm on the chart while the cost of getting out of it is rising.",
