 h_dex:"On-chain price across five DEXes",dex_size:"Order size",
 l_dex:"An eth_call is issued directly to each venue's router and quoter, without any third-party API, to compare which venue returns the most for the same size. Each venue is quoted against whichever dollar token it actually holds a pool in, with that token's own decimals.",
 n_dex:"Each venue is quoted as a single pool. Junoswap can split one order across several pools, which KUB Flow does not yet model, so its figure is a floor rather than the best price available. Kublerx prices against Bridged Tether USD rather than Bitkub-Peg KUSDT — a different contract, the same dollar.",
 w_dex:"Whether the on-chain price is worth using instead of the exchange, and where. The comparison is per size, because a venue that wins on 100 KUB can lose badly on 5,000: the gap between them is the cost of routing to the wrong one.",
 no_quote:"no pool",
 th_dex:"DEX",th_out:"USD out",th_px:"Per KUB",th_vs:"vs best",th_tok:"Quoted in",
 h_ex:"KUB held at Bitkub Exchange",
 l_ex:"Only the exchange's own wallets are counted here — its cold wallets and its active hot wallet — read every five minutes. Ecosystem funds, the stake vault and the company reserve are not the exchange's and are left to the supply panel. Transfers in and out are read from the chain, by day, in Bangkok time, and the history is walked backwards a page at a time from kubscan.",
 n_ex:"Days before the history walk reached them are marked as uncollected rather than drawn as zero flow, and are left out of both the total and the cumulative line. The exchange moves KUB between its own wallets too; only transfers crossing the boundary are counted. The line is read against the right-hand axis and starts from zero at the left edge of the range, so it shows the change across the period rather than a balance.",
 w_ex:"Whether coins are moving onto the exchange or away from it. Sustained flow onto an exchange puts sellable supply within reach of the order book; flow away from it takes supply out of immediate circulation. Neither predicts price, but both change what the book can absorb.",
 ex_in:"Onto the exchange",ex_out:"Off the exchange",ex_net:"Net out, period",
 ex_bal:"Held by the exchange",ex_nodata:"not collected",
 h_chain:"Chain activity",
 l_chain:"Daily totals from kubscan. Fees are fetched one day at a time and reach as far back as the backfill has walked. Transaction counts come from its chart endpoint, which returns the last 31 days and ignores any date range asked of it, so the line stops where that window does while the bars carry on.",
 n_chain:"Gas units are deliberately not shown. kubscan quotes a flat 25 gwei, but that is the price offered for a new transaction, not the average actually paid: on 19 Sep it measured 9,466,430,334 gas against 190.41 KUB of fees, an effective 20.1 gwei. Dividing fees by 25 gwei would understate gas by about a fifth, and there is no per-day gas figure to use instead.",
 w_chain:"How much the chain is actually being used, in fees paid and transactions settled. It is the demand side behind everything else on this page: a market's depth and an exchange's flow both sit on top of a chain that people are either using or not. The newest day here is the last one kubscan has closed, so it trails the running totals on their front page by a day.",
 ch_fees:"Fees paid, KUB",ch_tx:"Transactions",ch_avg:"Average fee per transaction",
 r_7d:"7d",r_1m:"1M",r_3m:"3M",r_1y:"1Y",
 h_treas:"Distribution of the coin supply",
 l_treas:"Measured against the whole coin supply, not only the wallets under observation, and from balances rather than transfers: the stake vault is a contract whose KUB moves as internal transactions that never appear in the transaction list, so the balance is the only reliable measure.",
 n_treas:"The burn address is excluded. kubscan credits it with more KUB than exists, which follows from how gas is accounted for rather than from any actual holder. Large holders are grouped by the label kubscan publishes for them; addresses it carries no label for are listed by address and counted as unidentified, not given an invented name.",
 w_treas:"How much of the supply is parked and where. Coins in a stake vault, a fund's cold wallet or the KKUB wrapper are not sitting on an order book, so the share that is genuinely free to trade is smaller than the total supply suggests.",
 g_stake:"Stake vault",g_fund:"Ecosystem & development funds",g_cold:"Bitkub Exchange wallets",
 g_kkub:"Wrapped as KKUB",g_reserve:"KUB Company Reserve",g_unid:"Unidentified large holders",g_rest:"Other holders",
 t_supply:"{watched} of {total} KUB held in the wallets under observation ({pct}%)",
 th_wallet:"Wallet",th_group:"Group",th_bal:"Balance, KUB",th_share:"Share",
 h_health:"Collection integrity",
 l_health:"Every collection round is recorded, whether it succeeds or fails, so gaps remain visible rather than hidden. Counts are compared against how many rounds the schedule should have produced in 24 hours.",
 w_health:"Whether the numbers above are standing on complete data. A collector that has been failing quietly turns every panel it feeds into a confident half-truth, so its record is kept where it can be checked.",
 th_job:"Collection job",th_runs:"Rounds, 24 h",th_fail:"Failed",th_state:"State",
 st_ok:"healthy",st_ramp:"ramping up",st_fail:"failed",
 fold_show:"Show",fold_hide:"Hide",health_sum:"{ok} of {n} jobs healthy",
 f1:"The figures on this page are measured by KUB Flow from the order book, the trade record and the chain. Where a figure originates elsewhere, the panel states so.",
 f2:"The order book is captured 60 levels deep; sizes beyond that depth cannot be priced from it. Windows longer than the data actually collected are labelled as such, and are never back-filled.",
 f3:"Not investment advice.",
